From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] src/lab-process-mail: Find work without the mail
 bookmark
To: lab@lists.p7x.dev
Cc: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: uvrwunuszmwxuvxsstxumxpmtzzqtwrz
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:14:00 +0000

The work revset kept the jj maildir outbox out by naming
mail@upstream, so retiring the mail bookmark would make every pass
fail on a revset that no longer resolves. Worse, the outbox commits
would then count as work and be rebased onto trunk.

Taking work only from the base's own line of history leaves out
anything that shares no history with it, the old outbox included,
whether or not the bookmark still exists.
---
change-id: uvrwunuszmwxuvxsstxumxpmtzzqtwrz

 src/lab-process-mail/lab-process-mail      |  8 ++---
 src/lab-process-mail/lab-process-mail_test | 34 +++++++++++++++-------
 src/lab-process-mail/prompt.md             |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/lab-process-mail/lab-process-mail b/src/lab-process-mail/lab-process-mail
index 0c53b67a..146e87a6 100755
--- a/src/lab-process-mail/lab-process-mail
+++ b/src/lab-process-mail/lab-process-mail
@@ -39,12 +39,12 @@ readonly BASE="${LAB_BASE_BRANCH:-trunk()}"
 readonly SENDERS="${LAB_PROCESS_MAIL_SENDERS:-pat@patmaddox.com pat@p7x.dev}"
 export NOTMUCH_PROFILE="${NOTMUCH_PROFILE:-lab-mail}"
 
-# Your commits off the base, less everything descended from the list.
-# The base and the list share no commit but root(), so the outbox is
-# left out however far the list has moved since it was built on.
+# Your commits off the base, in the base's own line of history. A
+# commit that shares no history with the base but root(), such as one
+# from the jj maildir that once carried the list, is left out.
 # Anything built on a published head other than the base is left where
 # it is; that covers your own patches once Pat publishes them.
-readonly WORK="mine() ~ ::(${BASE}) ~ (::mail@upstream ~ root())::
+readonly WORK="roots(::(${BASE}) ~ root()):: & mine() ~ ::(${BASE})
     ~ (immutable() ~ ::(${BASE}))::"
 
 err() {
